WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:02.250
Film Courage: Is someone writing for themselves
or for the industry?

00:00:02.250 --> 00:00:05.860
Lee Jessup: That’s a good question.

00:00:05.860 --> 00:00:09.790
Somebody is writing the stories that they
love, that they are passionate about.

00:00:09.790 --> 00:00:17.300
I don’t believe in writing to the market
because ultimately you will also be behind.

00:00:17.300 --> 00:00:20.720
What you’re writing now, if you’re with
whatever is happening in the industry, whatever

00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:25.179
is happening in the industry right now, in
six months it is going to be dated.

00:00:25.179 --> 00:00:29.470
So I think writing to the industry can be
a losing battle.

00:00:29.470 --> 00:00:34.020
While you should write with an awareness of
your audience (who you audience is) whether

00:00:34.020 --> 00:00:36.570
it’s television or film, who would watch
this show?

00:00:36.570 --> 00:00:38.350
Where would this show belong?

00:00:38.350 --> 00:00:40.360
What season does this film get released?

00:00:40.360 --> 00:00:41.680
Is this a summer blockbuster?

00:00:41.680 --> 00:00:43.200
Is this an end-of-year movie?

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:45.170
Is this a February movie?

00:00:45.170 --> 00:00:47.900
Is it going to be a movie for 16-to-24-year-olds?

00:00:47.900 --> 00:00:50.630
Or is it going to be a movie for 49-year-olds
and older?

00:00:50.630 --> 00:00:51.630
What are we talking about?

00:00:51.630 --> 00:00:55.470
You should be aware of all of those things
but you shouldn’t write to them.

00:00:55.470 --> 00:01:03.460
I think the moment when you try to engineer
your work toward something, it loses its brilliance.

00:01:03.460 --> 00:01:10.300
I know somebody (a manager) who was working
with his girlfriend to engineer a script for

00:01:10.300 --> 00:01:12.750
the blacklist, for the list (The Blacklist).

00:01:12.750 --> 00:01:16.090
Ultimately, that script was never finished
because it was engineered.

00:01:16.090 --> 00:01:19.259
And the manager then came back to me and said
“Yeah, we tried to engineer it.

00:01:19.259 --> 00:01:21.500
Clearly a bad idea.”

00:01:21.500 --> 00:01:24.749
So you have to listen to your heart song in
that sense.

00:01:24.749 --> 00:01:30.530
You have to really write the original, exciting
material that is uniquely yours that is the

00:01:30.530 --> 00:01:35.130
story you will do anything to tell with some
awareness of how the market will and won’t

00:01:35.130 --> 00:01:36.130
receive it.

00:01:36.130 --> 00:01:42.689
If you want to write a script that is going
to be full of singing and speaking eels, it’s

00:01:42.689 --> 00:01:45.359
likely going to be a challenge.

00:01:45.359 --> 00:01:47.929
But if you have to do it, do it.

00:01:47.929 --> 00:01:50.420
But write it in a way that is true for you.

00:01:50.420 --> 00:01:56.159
Write the story that you want to tell in a
way that is exciting to you but can be digested

00:01:56.159 --> 00:01:57.639
for the market that it’s for.

00:01:57.639 --> 00:01:58.005
Question for the Viewers: Do you write scripts
you know you can sell?

